-- Restore readable structure for the two migrated Google Docs rules.
-- The hash guard preserves any organiser edits made after import.
update public.events
set rules_html = $rules$<h2>Open division</h2><p>This season, our Open Division will feature 14 teams, with each team guaranteed 7 regular-season games, plus playoffs games.</p><h2>Season format</h2><ul><li>14 teams</li><li>Custom round robin format</li><li>7 games per team</li></ul><p>After the regular season:</p><h2>Open division 1</h2><ul><li>Seeds 1–8 advance to the division 1 playoffs</li></ul><h2>Open division 2</h2><ul><li>Seeds 9–12 advance to the division 2 playoffs</li><li>Seeds 13–14 are eliminated</li></ul><h2>Awards</h2><p>Division 1 champions: Championship trophy, championship caps, championship rings plus $600 less next season</p><p>Division 1 1st runner up: Trophy, medals</p><p>Division 2 champions: Championship trophy, championship caps, plus $200 less next season</p><p>Open division league MVP: Trophy</p><p>Division 1 finals MVP: Trophy</p><p>Division 2 finals MVP: Trophy</p><p>Division 1 mythical five: Trophies</p><p>Division 2 mythical five: Trophies</p><h2>Baliklaro 35+ division</h2><p>We have a few changes for our Baliklaro 35+ Division this season.</p><p>We will have a total of 7 stacked teams, which means each team will have one bye during the schedule.</p><p>For teams with a bye, we’re offering 1 free hour at the High School Gym on that Saturday if you’d like to use the time for team practice. Please let us know in advance if you’d like to book a slot.</p><p>Because of this schedule adjustment, we have also reduced the Baliklaro 35+ entry fee from $1,350 to $1,250.</p><p>Season Format:</p><ul><li>7 teams</li><li>Single round robin</li><li>6 games per team</li><li>Seeds 1–6 advance to the playoffs</li><li>7th seed is eliminated</li></ul><h2>Awards</h2><p>Baliklaro 35+ champions: Championship trophy, championship caps, championship rings plus $600 less next season</p><p>Baliklaro 35+ 1st runner up: Trophy, medals</p><p>League MVP: Trophy</p><p>Finals MVP: Trophy</p><p>Mythical five: Trophies</p>$rules$
where legacy_firebase_id = '-P08tvBDGZKmSa6AGnNm'
  and md5(rules_html) = '10687daa0d628e520b074cd03c728635';

update public.events
set rules_html = $rules$<h2>2026 Brotherhood league – rules and regulations</h2><h2>1. Team line-up</h2><p>All Active Members Only (See Player Eligibility Requirement on Roster Form).</p><p>Each player must submit a signed individual Eligibility Declaration Letter. The allowable number of players per team is min. 8 to max. 15 players as long as the team will follow the 5 Minutes Rule. All players must play a minimum of 5 minutes per period when the rule is in effect. If there are teams with more than 15 players, only maximum of 15 players will be allowed to play in a given game schedule.</p><h2>2. Uniforms</h2><p>No player will be allowed to play without wearing the official team uniform/colour (both shorts &amp; shirt) during the game.</p><h2>3. Tempers/arguments/fights</h2><p>Coaches and Technical Committee will be diligent regarding Tempers, Arguments and Fights in the game.</p><p>Reminders/Warnings will be given to both teams before the start of every game.</p><p>During the game, automatic technical foul and game ejection will be given to any of the following reasons (but not limited to): trash talking, swearing, arguing with the referees, fighting (in any form). Referees’ discretion will be used.</p><p>A player who commits three (3) technical fouls/ejections in the elimination round will automatically be out for the rest of the season. No exceptions – you have been warned!</p><h2>4. Duration of the game:</h2><h2>Elimination round:</h2><ul><li>Continuous 20 minutes for the first half and 24 minutes in the 2nd half except for the last 4 minutes of the second half. (Stop clock on all timeouts). stop clock on substitutions and free throws in the last 4 minutes of the second half only.</li></ul><ul><li>Overtime duration: overtime period is two (2) minutes stop clock. Penalty shot after 3 fouls. Each team will have one 30 second timeout in overtime period.</li></ul><ul><li>Official substitution: *5 minute rule - automatic substitution every 5 minutes (2nd 5 or 3rd 5 if applicable) to allow all players to play in the first and second half. It will be coach's decision after.</li></ul><ul><li>On injuries, the substitute will be the player who has not played yet based on the "5 Minute Rule". This rule applies in the 1st half and 2nd half. If a player requests to be relieved for various reasons (fatigue, injury, etc.), he may do so during a dead ball situation and by communicating with the referees. Substitutions should be based on the "5 Minute Rule"</li></ul><ul><li>Timeout: Each team can call for (2) 30 sec. timeouts in the first half and (3) 30 sec. timeouts in the second half. Substitutions can also be made at that time. Only the coach or the captain ball is allowed to ask for a timeout at the official's table. A technical foul will be given to the team who will call a timeout after the allowed numbers of timeouts have been used. Two (2) free throws will be given to the other team plus ball possession. Injuries and referees timeouts are 20 seconds only.</li></ul><h2>Play-offs semis and finals:</h2><p>20 minutes running time in the 1st half 20 minutes Stop clock in the 2nd half.</p><p>Stop clock for any substitutions and free throws for the duration of game.</p><ul><li>5 minutes rule applies in the 1st half only, 2nd half will be coaches decision.</li></ul><ul><li>For substitution, all players should report to the official's table. Table officials will only allow substitution when there is a dead ball situation.</li></ul><ul><li>Timeout: There are two (2) timeouts for the 1st half Three (3) timeouts for the 2nd half. Each timeout is 30 sec.</li></ul><ul><li>Overtime duration: overtime period is three (3) minutes stop clock Penalty shot after 3 fouls. Each team will have one 30 seconds timeout in overtime period. Only the coach or the captain ball is allowed to ask for a timeout at the official's table. A technical foul will be given to the team who will call a timeout after the allowed numbers of timeouts have been used. Two (2) free throws will be given to the other team plus ball possession. Injuries and referees timeouts are 20 seconds only.</li></ul><h2>5. Shot clock:</h2><p>30 second shot clock is in effect at possession of the ball. Shot clock will reset when the ball hits the rim or after a foul was committed.</p><h2>6. Backcourt violation:</h2><p>Backcourt violation is 10 seconds.</p><h2>7. Fouls:</h2><p>There are shooting and non-shooting fouls. Shooting fouls will result to 2 free throws. Non-shooting fouls are just side out.</p><h2>8. Team fouls:</h2><p>After 8th team foul, two (2) free throws will be given to the other team.</p><h2>9. Personal fouls:</h2><p>Each player is allowed 5 personal fouls.</p><h2>10. Technical foul:</h2><p>A technical foul will result to one (1) free throw and ball possession.</p><p>Technical fouls will be called for the following reasons (but not limited to): trash talking, swearing, arguing with the referees, fighting (in any form). Referee's discretion will be used.</p><p>Refer to Item 3. Tempers/Arguments/Fights for technical fouls and ejection.</p><h2>11. Flagrant foul:</h2><p>Flagrant foul may be called by the referees if the intention of the player is to cause harm or injury to another player.</p><p>Flagrant foul will result to the player taken out of the playing court.</p><p>One free throw will be given to the other player and ball possession to his team.</p><p>The incident will be reviewed by a technical committee composed of representatives from all the teams.</p><p>The team rep whose player is the subject of a disciplinary action will be allowed to take part in the discussion but will be asked to abstain in the decision making.</p><p>The first flagrant foul of a player may result to a one game suspension.</p><p>Two flagrant fouls by the same player may result to the player being suspended for the remainder of the games.</p><h2>12. Winner by default:</h2><p>Each team will be given 5 minutes grace period to complete the required number of players (five players).</p><p>The team who fails to complete after the 5 minutes grace period will have their game considered as "loss by default".</p><p>The final score will be 20 - 0 in favor of the opposing/complete team.</p><p>$50 Penalty for the Defaulting Team.</p><p>Attendance will still be recorded for both teams.</p><h2>13. Table committee assignments:</h2><p>YFC’s to be paid as table committee in all the games. YFC will be from the venue Chapter but others are also welcome if there are not enough YFC to cover that particular week. Coordination with host team reps required.</p><h2>14. General basketball rules:</h2><p>Travelling, over the back fouls, charging fouls, technical fouls, 3 sec. in the paint, 5 sec. to inbound the ball, 10 sec. to bring the ball to half court, and 30 sec. shot clock. Most recent FIBA Basketball Rules will apply if not stated above.</p><p>Team Representative is trusted to discuss these rules with his Team before the tournament begins. * Referees will be informed by the Games Committee.</p><h2>15. Power play:</h2><p>N/a</p><h2>16. Eligibility to play in playoffs:</h2><p>Each player must have played a minimum of three (3) games in the elimination round in order for him to be allowed to play in the playoffs, semis &amp; finals.</p><p>Committee and team reps to confirm attendance. This includes attendance on a forfeited game due to default. Attendance of the “reserves” (players in excess of 15 players) will still be recorded.</p><h2>Mechanics of the game:</h2><p>Single round robin system in the elimination round.</p><p>Playoffs: (Top 8 teams will qualify for Quarter-Finals knock out game) Quarter-Finals: (Bracket 1) #1 vs #8, #4 vs #5 (Bracket 2) #3 vs #6, #2 vs #7 Semi-Finals 1st game Winners on Bracket 1 2ND game Winners on Bracket 2 Finals 1st game - 3rd place L1 vs L2 2nd game – Championship W1 vs W2</p><h2>Note:</h2><p>In case of a tie between two (2) teams, the winner over the other rule shall apply.</p><p>In case of three (3) or more ties, the quotient system shall apply. Only the games among themselves shall be considered. Quotient = Points for / Points against.</p>$rules$
where legacy_firebase_id = '-P13BNr-wtp2IdjiL2Hz'
  and md5(rules_html) = '2c351c4a81873858c8d108f2ce756317';
